      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for gzip",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for gzip fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-41992: global buffer overflow in the LZH decompression logic due to improper reuse of shared global state\n  between different decompression formats within a single execution (bsc#1269623).\n- crafted LZW file followed by a crafted LZH file can cause an out-of-bounds memory buffer access (bsc#1272554).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
